**Inconsistency: Missing nil guard on `Score`/`ScorePluginConf`**

`getQuotaCpuUsageScore` and `getQuotaMemMbUsageScore` in `utils.go` guard against `config.GetConfig().Scheduler == nil`, but this function accesses `schedConf.Score.ScorePluginConf.RealTimeWeightedAverage` at line 105 without checking if `Score` or `ScorePluginConf` is nil. If `Scheduler.Score` were ever nil (unlikely in production after init, but possible in tests with partial configs), this would panic.

Consider adding nil guards for consistency with `utils.go`:

```go
schedConf := config.GetConfig().Scheduler
if schedConf == nil || schedConf.Score == nil || schedConf.Score.ScorePluginConf == nil {
    return 0
}
sconf := schedConf.Score.ScorePluginConf.RealTimeWeightedAverage
if sconf == nil {
    return 0
}
```

