review_comments.body:
**Suggestion: Avoid redundant `DeepCopy` when the trace was just allocated**

When `rt` is nil and the code synthesizes a fresh `RequestTrace`, calling `rt.DeepCopy()` on line 207 allocates a second `RequestTrace` (~320 bytes) and discards the original. Since the newly allocated trace has no prior context to protect from mutation, you could pass it directly to `WithRequestTrace` and avoid the extra allocation.

```go
if rt == nil {
    // ... synthesize rt ...
    detached = CubeLog.WithRequestTrace(detached, rt)
    return log.WithLogger(detached, log.G(ctx).WithFields(fields))
}
detached = CubeLog.WithRequestTrace(detached, rt.DeepCopy())
return log.WithLogger(detached, log.G(ctx).WithFields(fields))
```

Minor optimization, but the savings is exact: one ~320B heap allocation per nil-trace call (reconciler tick, image job start).

