**Suggestion:** `json.Marshal` error is silently discarded here. If the config struct contains un-marshalable fields (e.g. non-serializable types sneak in via `Config`), this writes a zero-value config into the artifact record with no warning. Consider at least logging the error:

```go
configJSON, err := json.Marshal(configInfo.Config)
if err != nil {
    cleanup()
    return nil, fmt.Errorf("marshal image config: %w", err)
}
```

